00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.830
FELIPE HOFFA: My
name is Felipe Hoffa.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.270
You are interested
in visualizing data.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.190
Prepare to rewind.

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.620
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:14.825
For years, I've used
BigQuery and public data

00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:16.870
sets to publish
interesting articles.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.810
And I've used many different
visualization tools.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.660
But there was still
a space in my life

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.240
until Data Studio showed up.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.190
Google Data Studio is totally
free for you and for me.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.140
And I can use it to publish
interactive visualizations

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.100
online.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.470
And it's really easy to connect
it to many different sources,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.330
including BigQuery.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.000
So that's what I did.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.980
I analyzed data with BigQuery.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.900
I connected it to Data Studio.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.940
I made my dashboards
interactive.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.010
And I published them online.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.050
You can embed a Data
Studio dashboard anywhere,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.530
including some of the most
popular plugin platforms.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.710
But there are some challenges.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:00.250
As you know, BigQuery allows
you to analyze huge amounts

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.350
of data in very few seconds.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.950
And it only charge to you
for each query you run.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.690
And it has a free monthly tier.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.030
So you might end up
paying nothing at all.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.910
But if you connect BigQuery
to a popular dashboard,

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.670
then your users may
end up generating a lot

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.500
of queries on your behalf.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.550
And that means you can end
up with a huge BigQuery bill.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.670
We don't want that.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.650
So I asked the
developer advocate

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.160
for Data Studio, Minhaz
Kazi, to join me on state

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.640
to share our best strategies for
publishing dashboards with Data

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.450
Studio and BigQuery.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.690
For example, the
easiest way to avoid

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.450
pushing new queries from
Data Studio to BigQuery

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.650
is to materialize the results of
your queries into Data Studio.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.650
That's right, once you
have the BigQuery results

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.630
or table you want
to visualize, you

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.390
can use the Extract
button to do so.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.930
And Data Studio will offer you
an easy way to keep and refresh

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.160
a copy of this data.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.920
But right now, that feature
is still in development.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.960
And it will be subject
to certain limitations.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.660
So we also shared
some other options

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.940
to create an inexpensive
layer between Data Studio

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.050
and BigQuery.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.770
For example, you can
use G Suite Apps Script

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.780
to schedule queries and have the
results pushed to Google Cloud

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.030
Storage.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.820
You can then connect Data
Studio to that file, which

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.280
will be refreshed
based on your schedule.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.440
And your users will be able to
quickly explore the results.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.160
But this works only up to
a certain size of results.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.350
In other cases, it may
make a lot of sense

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.010
to use a database that
supports lookup by key.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.740
Once you know that your
visualization will all

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.410
require key lookups
to retrieve data,

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.570
instead of scanning
a table in BigQuery,

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.480
you can connect Data Studio
to a traditional database

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.540
and just get the
individual rows out of it.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.390
In this case, I exported
the BigQuery results

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.810
to a MySQL database
hosted on Cloud SQL.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.820
I added the required indexes.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.340
And we got quick,
inexpensive results.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.890
But sometimes you might
have more complex needs--

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:59.620
for example, when you
want to make a data

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.350
source available to
many users and let them

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.170
build their own
customized visualizations.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.840
In that case, you can
create a Data Studio custom

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.890
connector with Apps Script and
design your own caching logic

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.010
within it.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.190
In the full talk, you
can see this in action

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:19.090
with Minhaz's example, where he
created a connector that anyone

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.250
can use with just
a couple clicks.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.490
And they get a custom and
customizable visualization

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.740
with fresh data,
hosted in BigQuery,

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.040
without any need of
coding, SQL or otherwise.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.100
In summary., if you want to
connect BigQuery and Data

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.470
Studio to create an
interactive dashboard,

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.000
and you want to
make this dashboard

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.670
available for everyone,
remember to think

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.855
about what kind of layer you
want to have between BigQuery

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.500
and Data Studio.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.520
And stay tuned.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.410
Because at Google, we
are always thinking

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.620
about how to make this
connection even more powerful.

